Style Guide Suggestion: The style guide prefers avoiding let statements. Consider using an IIFE or ternary expression to avoid the mutable variable. For example:

const cutoffTime = (() => {
  if (days === undefined) return 0
  if (days === 0) {
    const now = new Date()
    now.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0)
    return now.getTime()
  }
  return Date.now() - days * MS_IN_DAY
})()
This is just a suggestion - if you feel the current let approach is simpler/clearer, feel free to keep it.
